    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22386": {
      "title": "Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Course Lecturer)",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Course Lecturer) - Winter 2027 Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Course Lecturer) - Winter 2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Course Lecturer) - Winter 2027 Posting Number PTAP3569P Department/Unit Biology Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Job Summary & Key Responsibilities The part-time academic is responsible for delivering lectures in BIOL / MARI 3371 during the Winter 2027 term. This course is taught from a comparative perspective and covers animal respiratory and circulatory systems, metabolic rates, muscle function, and osmoregulation. The successful applicant will be responsible for designing, administering (including exam invigilation), and grading all lecture assessments. The part-time academic is also responsible for communicating with the course laboratory instructor to coordinate lecture and laboratory components, facilitating approved academic accommodations related to the lecture component of the course, and providing support to students through office hours and individual consultations, as needed. Lectures are scheduled from 10:30 a.m. to 11:30 a.m. on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays. The successful applicant should expect to spend considerable time before and after the official course dates preparing instructional materials and grading assessments. Due to operational requirements, the successful applicant is required to work in person on campus. The position reports to the Chair of the Department of Biology. Qualifications/Requirements of Position Advanced degree in biology or marine biology, related to the content of the course. Preference will be given to candidates with previous university teaching experience in the subject of the course. Applications should include a letter and an up-to-date CV. First-time applicants should provide evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as summary of relevant course evaluations) and must provide the names of two references. Salary Range/Pay Rate Per CUPE Collective Agreement Additional Information All offers of employment as a Part-Time Academic are conditional upon sufficient student enrolment in the course and approval by the University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Term of appointment January - April 2027 Open Date 10/20/2026 Close Date 11/03/2026 Open Until Filled Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22348 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Teaching Statement Teaching Dossier Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
