    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22385": {
      "title": "Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Lab Instructor)",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Lab Instructor) - Winter 2027 Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Lab Instructor) - Winter 2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Part-Time Academic (BIOL/MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology Lab Instructor) - Winter 2027 Posting Number PTAP3568P Department/Unit Biology Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Job Summary & Key Responsibilities The part-time academic is responsible for coordinating BIOL / MARI 3371: Laboratory in Comparative Animal Physiology during the Winter 2027 term. Duties include developing and managing the course Brightspace site; hiring and supervising TAs; communicating with the course lecturer to coordinate lecture and laboratory components; addressing student concerns; facilitating approved academic accommodations; invigilating tests and examinations; and submitting final grades. The successful applicant is also responsible for delivering the laboratory component of the course, which covers aspects of animal respiration, circulation, metabolic rate, muscle function, and osmoregulation. This role involves providing support to students on an individual basis as needed. Laboratory sessions are scheduled from 2:30 p.m. to 5:30 p.m. on Tuesdays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. The successful applicant should expect to spend considerable time before and after the official course dates preparing laboratory materials, assessments, and course logistics, as well as completing grading and other administrative responsibilities following the end of the term. Due to operational requirements, the successful applicant is required to work in person on campus. The position reports to the Chair of the Department of Biology. Qualifications/Requirements of Position Advanced degree in biology or marine biology, related to the content of the course. Preference will be given to candidates with previous university teaching experience in the subject of the course. Applications should include a cover letter and an up-to-date CV. First-time applicants should provide evidence of teaching effectiveness (such as summary of relevant course evaluations) and must provide the names of two references. Salary Range/Pay Rate Per CUPE Collective Agreement Additional Information All offers of employment as a Part-Time Academic are conditional upon sufficient student enrolment in the course and approval by the University. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Term of appointment January - April 2027 Open Date 10/20/2026 Close Date 11/03/2026 Open Until Filled Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22347 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Teaching Statement Teaching Dossier Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
